{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-big-bang-state","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:big-bang-state","kind":"definition","title":"Big bang state (degree-$0$ trivial configuration)","tags":["big-bang-state","jet-horizon","initial-conditions","degree-zero","deep-quantum"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BigBangState","text":"big-bang-state.md","leanSource":"big-bang-state.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:big-bang-state\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U \\subset M_0</code> be an affine chart carrying a bundle initial condition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_0 = \\sum_i (p_i, H_i)</code>. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_0</code> is a <strong>big bang state</strong> if its degree-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> algebra is trivial:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Gamma\\!\\bigl(U, A_0|_{\\mathcal{S}_0}\\bigr) = 0.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/big-bang-state.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.12.3","page":"b/def-big-bang-state","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BigBangState","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/big-bang-state.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
